<title>UK: Eksportfinans sets 20 bln yen note.</title>
<headline>Eksportfinans sets 20 bln yen note.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following dual-currency note</p>
<p>was announced by joint lead managers Kankaku (Europe) Ltd and</p>
<p>DKB International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EKSPORTFINANS</p>
<p> AMT    20 BLN YEN    COUPON     4.30	MATURITY    15.AUG.97</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.0     PAY DATE    15.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.55	LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AA1/AAA   DENOMS (M) ONE	 SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.05	SELL CONC  0.50	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	FINAL REDEMPTION A) IF DURING THE PERIOD 15.MAY.97</p>
<p>		TO 08.AUG.97, THE YEN/DOLAR RATE IS EQUAL TO OR LESS</p>
<p>		THAN 119.25 YEN/$1.00 THE REDEMPTION AMOUNT WILL BE</p>
<p>		$7,877.12 PER NOTE OR OTHERWISE B) REDEMPTION AMOUNT</p>
<p>		WILL BE BY 1.0 MLN YEN PER NOTE.</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
